<DemoExample Title="Basic" RazorCode="@example1RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example1CsharpCode" Id="example1">
    <div>
        Each item is an icon over its text, and a link when it has a <b>Url</b>. In the default <b>Automatic</b> mode
        the item whose URL matches the current page is selected and marked <code>aria-current="page"</code>.
    </div>
    <br />
    <div class="container">
        <BitNavBar Items="basicNavBarItems" />
    </div>
</DemoExample>

<DemoExample Title="Disabled" RazorCode="@example2RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example2CsharpCode" Id="example2" PreventRenderForMcpClient>
    <div>
        <b>IsEnabled</b> disables the whole navbar or a single item. A disabled item loses its link and its tab stop,
        and is announced as dimmed.
    </div>
    <br />
    <div>Disabled navbar:</div><br />
    <div class="container short">
        <BitNavBar Items="basicNavBarItems" IsEnabled="false" />
    </div>
    <br /><br />
    <div>Disabled item:</div><br />
    <div class="container short">
        <BitNavBar Items="basicNavBarItemsDisabled" />
    </div>
</DemoExample>

<DemoExample Title="Manual Mode" RazorCode="@example3RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example3CsharpCode" Id="example3" PreventRenderForMcpClient>
    <div>
        In the <b>Manual</b> mode clicks select the items instead of the URL, for a navbar that switches panels of one
        page. <b>DefaultSelectedItem</b> sets the starting item.
    </div>
    <br />
    <div class="container">
        <BitNavBar Mode="BitNavMode.Manual"
                   Items="basicNavBarItems"
                   DefaultSelectedItem="basicNavBarItems[0]" />
    </div>
</DemoExample>

<DemoExample Title="URL Matching" RazorCode="@example4RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example4CsharpCode" Id="example4" PreventRenderForMcpClient>
    <div>
        <b>Match</b> (per navbar, or per item) compares URLs <b>Exact</b>ly (the default), by <b>Prefix</b>, as a
        <b>Wildcard</b> pattern (<b>?</b>, <b>*</b> within a segment, <b>**</b> across segments) or as a <b>Regex</b>.
        Exact and Prefix ignore case and a trailing slash. <b>AdditionalUrls</b> gives an item more URLs to match.
        All of these are matched against the URL of this page.
    </div>
    <br />
    <div>Exact (the default):</div><br />
    <div class="container short">
        <BitNavBar Items="exactMatchItems" />
    </div>
    <br /><br />
    <div>Prefix:</div><br />
    <div class="container short">
        <BitNavBar Items="prefixMatchItems" Match="BitNavMatch.Prefix" />
    </div>
    <br /><br />
    <div>Wildcard:</div><br />
    <div class="container short">
        <BitNavBar Items="wildcardMatchItems" />
    </div>
    <br /><br />
    <div>Regex:</div><br />
    <div class="container short">
        <BitNavBar Items="regexMatchItems" />
    </div>
    <br /><br />
    <div>AdditionalUrls:</div><br />
    <div class="container short">
        <BitNavBar Items="additionalUrlsItems" />
    </div>
</DemoExample>

<DemoExample Title="Labels" RazorCode="@example5RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example5CsharpCode" Id="example5" PreventRenderForMcpClient>
    <div>
        <b>IconOnly</b> hides every label, <b>HideUnselectedText</b> keeps only the selected one's, and
        <b>InlineText</b> puts the label beside the icon. A hidden label still names its item for screen readers.
    </div>
    <br />
    <div>IconOnly:</div><br />
    <div class="container short">
        <BitNavBar Items="basicNavBarItems" IconOnly />
    </div>
    <br /><br />
    <div>HideUnselectedText:</div><br />
    <div class="container short">
        <BitNavBar HideUnselectedText
                   Mode="BitNavMode.Manual"
                   Items="basicNavBarItems"
                   DefaultSelectedItem="basicNavBarItems[0]" />
    </div>
    <br /><br />
    <div>InlineText:</div><br />
    <div class="container short">
        <BitNavBar Items="basicNavBarItems" InlineText />
    </div>
</DemoExample>

<DemoExample Title="Width & Alignment" RazorCode="@example6RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example6CsharpCode" Id="example6" PreventRenderForMcpClient>
    <div>
        <b>FitWidth</b> shrinks the navbar to its content and <b>FullWidth</b> stretches it over its container.
        <b>Justified</b> gives every item an equal share, and <b>Alignment</b> packs or spreads the items along the bar.
    </div>
    <br />
    <div>FitWidth:</div><br />
    <div class="container short">
        <BitNavBar Items="basicNavBarItems" FitWidth />
    </div>
    <br /><br />
    <div>FullWidth:</div><br />
    <div class="container short">
        <BitNavBar Items="basicNavBarItems" FullWidth />
    </div>
    <br /><br />
    <div>Justified (labels of unequal length):</div><br />
    <div class="container short">
        <BitNavBar Items="unevenNavBarItems" Justified />
    </div>
    <br /><br />
    <div>Alignment Center:</div><br />
    <div class="container short">
        <BitNavBar Alignment="BitAlignment.Center" Items="basicNavBarItems" />
    </div>
    <br /><br />
    <div>Alignment SpaceBetween:</div><br />
    <div class="container short">
        <BitNavBar Alignment="BitAlignment.SpaceBetween" Items="basicNavBarItems" />
    </div>
</DemoExample>

<DemoExample Title="Selection" RazorCode="@example7RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example7CsharpCode" Id="example7" PreventRenderForMcpClient>
    <div>
        <b>SelectedIconName</b> (or <b>SelectedIcon</b>) swaps the selected item to a filled glyph. <b>Filled</b> fills
        the hovered and selected item with the <b>Color</b>, and <b>Indicator</b> adds a <b>Line</b> along its edge or
        a <b>Pill</b> behind its icon - cues beyond color alone.
    </div>
    <br />
    <div>SelectedIconName:</div><br />
    <div class="container short">
        <BitNavBar Mode="BitNavMode.Manual"
                   Items="selectedIconItems"
                   DefaultSelectedItem="selectedIconItems[0]" />
    </div>
    <br /><br />
    <div>Filled:</div><br />
    <div class="container short">
        <BitNavBar Filled
                   Mode="BitNavMode.Manual"
                   Items="selectedIconItems"
                   DefaultSelectedItem="selectedIconItems[0]" />
    </div>
    <br /><br />
    <div>Line indicator:</div><br />
    <div class="container short">
        <BitNavBar Indicator="BitNavBarIndicator.Line"
                   Mode="BitNavMode.Manual"
                   Items="selectedIconItems"
                   DefaultSelectedItem="selectedIconItems[0]" />
    </div>
    <br /><br />
    <div>Pill indicator:</div><br />
    <div class="container short">
        <BitNavBar Indicator="BitNavBarIndicator.Pill"
                   Mode="BitNavMode.Manual"
                   Items="selectedIconItems"
                   DefaultSelectedItem="selectedIconItems[0]" />
    </div>
    <br /><br />
    <div>Pill indicator, Filled:</div><br />
    <div class="container short">
        <BitNavBar Indicator="BitNavBarIndicator.Pill"
                   Filled
                   Mode="BitNavMode.Manual"
                   Items="selectedIconItems"
                   DefaultSelectedItem="selectedIconItems[0]" />
    </div>
</DemoExample>

<DemoExample Title="Scrollable" RazorCode="@example8RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example8CsharpCode" Id="example8">
    <div>
        <b>Scrollable</b> scrolls the items instead of squeezing them (scrollbar hidden) and brings the selected item
        into view whenever the selection moves - here from the button.
    </div>
    <br />
    <BitButton OnClick="@(() => scrollableSelectedItem = scrollableNavBarItems[^1])">Select the last item</BitButton>
    <br /><br />
    <div class="container">
        <BitNavBar TItem="BitNavBarItem"
                   Scrollable
                   Mode="BitNavMode.Manual"
                   Items="scrollableNavBarItems"
                   @bind-SelectedItem="scrollableSelectedItem" />
    </div>
    <br />
    Selected item: @scrollableSelectedItem?.Text
</DemoExample>

<DemoExample Title="Header & Footer" RazorCode="@example9RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example9CsharpCode" Id="example9">
    <div>
        <b>HeaderTemplate</b> and <b>FooterTemplate</b> render content before and after the items, outside their list,
        so a screen reader does not count it among the destinations.
    </div>
    <br />
    <div class="container">
        <BitNavBar Items="basicNavBarItems">
            <HeaderTemplate>
                <BitImage Src="/_content/Bit.BlazorUI.Demo.Client.Core/images/bit-logo.svg" Width="32" Alt="bit" />
            </HeaderTemplate>
            <FooterTemplate>
                <BitButton IconOnly Title="More" Variant="BitVariant.Text" IconName="@BitIconName.More" />
            </FooterTemplate>
        </BitNavBar>
    </div>
</DemoExample>

<DemoExample Title="Vertical" RazorCode="@example10RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example10CsharpCode" Id="example10" PreventRenderForMcpClient>
    <div>
        <b>Vertical</b> turns the navbar into a navigation rail (usually with <b>FitWidth</b>). Everything above
        applies: the <b>Line</b> runs down the leading edge and <b>Scrollable</b> scrolls down the rail.
    </div>
    <br />
    <div>Basic:</div><br />
    <div class="container">
        <BitNavBar Items="basicNavBarItems" Vertical FitWidth />
    </div>
    <br /><br />
    <div>InlineText and Line indicator:</div><br />
    <div class="container">
        <BitNavBar Vertical
                   FitWidth
                   InlineText
                   Indicator="BitNavBarIndicator.Line"
                   Items="basicNavBarItems"
                   Mode="BitNavMode.Manual"
                   DefaultSelectedItem="basicNavBarItems[0]" />
    </div>
    <br /><br />
    <div>IconOnly, centered, with header and footer:</div><br />
    <div class="container">
        <BitNavBar Vertical FitWidth IconOnly Alignment="BitAlignment.Center" Items="basicNavBarItems">
            <HeaderTemplate>
                <BitButton IconOnly Title="New" IconName="@BitIconName.Add" />
            </HeaderTemplate>
            <FooterTemplate>
                <BitButton IconOnly Title="Settings" Variant="BitVariant.Text" IconName="@BitIconName.Settings" />
            </FooterTemplate>
        </BitNavBar>
    </div>
    <br /><br />
    <div>Scrollable:</div><br />
    <div class="container">
        <BitNavBar Scrollable
                   Vertical
                   FitWidth
                   Style="height:16rem"
                   Mode="BitNavMode.Manual"
                   Items="scrollableNavBarItems" />
    </div>
</DemoExample>

<DemoExample Title="Badge" RazorCode="@example11RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example11CsharpCode" Id="example11" PreventRenderForMcpClient>
    <div>
        <b>Badge</b> puts a count on the icon and <b>Dot</b> marks it without one. The badge is folded into the item's
        name ("Inbox (12)"); <b>BadgeAriaLabel</b> replaces that text, and is the only way a dot is announced.
    </div>
    <br />
    <div class="container">
        <BitNavBar Items="badgeNavBarItems" />
    </div>
</DemoExample>

<DemoExample Title="Templates" RazorCode="@example12RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example12CsharpCode" Id="example12">
    <div>
        <b>ItemTemplate</b> replaces the content of every item and an item's <b>Template</b> its own. With a
        <b>TemplateRenderMode</b> (or <b>ItemTemplateRenderMode</b>) of <b>Replace</b> the template replaces the whole
        item, for an item that is a control of its own; it then owns its clicks, focus and name.
    </div>
    <br />
    <div>ItemTemplate:</div><br />
    <div class="container short">
        <BitNavBar Items="basicNavBarItems">
            <ItemTemplate Context="item">
                <BitText Typography="BitTypography.Caption1" Color="BitColor.Warning">@item.Text</BitText>
                <BitIcon IconName="@item.IconName" Color="BitColor.Success" />
            </ItemTemplate>
        </BitNavBar>
    </div>
    <br /><br />
    <div>Item's template:</div><br />
    <div class="container short">
        <BitNavBar Items="templateNavBarItems" />
    </div>
    <br /><br />
    <div>Replaced item template:</div><br />
    <div class="container short">
        <BitNavBar Mode="BitNavMode.Manual"
                   Items="replacedTemplateNavBarItems"
                   DefaultSelectedItem="replacedTemplateNavBarItems[0]" />
    </div>
</DemoExample>

<DemoExample Title="Events" RazorCode="@example13RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example13CsharpCode" Id="example13">
    <div>
        <b>OnItemClick</b> fires on a click and <b>OnSelectItem</b> when the selection moves. Both skip the already
        selected item unless <b>Reselectable</b> is set - for a bar that scrolls its page to the top on a second tap.
    </div>
    <br />
    <BitToggle @bind-Value="reselectable" Label="Reselectable" Inline />
    <br />
    <div class="container short">
        <BitNavBar Items="basicNavBarItems"
                   Mode="BitNavMode.Manual"
                   Reselectable="reselectable"
                   OnItemClick="(BitNavBarItem item) => { eventsClickedItem = item; clickCount++; }"
                   OnSelectItem="(BitNavBarItem item) => { eventsSelectedItem = item; selectCount++; }" />
    </div>
    <br />
    <div>Clicked item: @eventsClickedItem?.Text (@clickCount clicks)</div>
    <div>Selected item: @eventsSelectedItem?.Text (@selectCount selections)</div>
</DemoExample>

<DemoExample Title="Binding" RazorCode="@example14RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example14CsharpCode" Id="example14">
    <div><b>SelectedItem</b> binds both ways, so the selection can be read and written from outside the navbar.</div>
    <br />
    <div class="container short">
        <BitNavBar TItem="BitNavBarItem"
                   @bind-SelectedItem="twoWaySelectedItem"
                   Items="basicNavBarItems"
                   Mode="BitNavMode.Manual" />
    </div>
    <br />
    Selected item: @twoWaySelectedItem?.Text
    <br /><br />
    <BitChoiceGroup Horizontal Items="@choiceGroupItems" @bind-Value="@twoWaySelectedItem" />
</DemoExample>

<DemoExample Title="Keyboard" RazorCode="@example15RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example15CsharpCode" Id="example15" PreventRenderForMcpClient>
    <div>
        The arrow keys, <b>Home</b> and <b>End</b> move the focus (flipped in RTL, skipping disabled items). By default
        every item is a tab stop; <b>SingleTabStop</b> makes the bar one stop like a toolbar. <b>WrapNavigation</b>
        wraps at the ends, and <b>SelectOnFocus</b> moves the selection with the focus (Manual mode).
    </div>
    <br />
    <div>SingleTabStop:</div><br />
    <div class="container short">
        <BitNavBar SingleTabStop
                   Mode="BitNavMode.Manual"
                   Items="basicNavBarItems"
                   DefaultSelectedItem="basicNavBarItems[1]" />
    </div>
    <br /><br />
    <div>WrapNavigation:</div><br />
    <div class="container short">
        <BitNavBar WrapNavigation
                   SingleTabStop
                   Mode="BitNavMode.Manual"
                   Items="basicNavBarItems"
                   DefaultSelectedItem="basicNavBarItems[1]" />
    </div>
    <br /><br />
    <div>SelectOnFocus:</div><br />
    <div class="container short">
        <BitNavBar SelectOnFocus
                   SingleTabStop
                   Mode="BitNavMode.Manual"
                   Items="basicNavBarItems"
                   DefaultSelectedItem="basicNavBarItems[1]" />
    </div>
</DemoExample>

<DemoExample Title="Dynamic Items" RazorCode="@example16RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example16CsharpCode" Id="example16">
    <div>
        <b>Items</b> is re-read on every render, so changes to the same list show up at once; the selection survives
        while its item is still there.
    </div>
    <br />
    <BitStack Horizontal>
        <BitButton OnClick="AddDynamicItem">Add item</BitButton>
        <BitButton OnClick="RemoveDynamicItem">Remove item</BitButton>
        <BitButton OnClick="ReverseDynamicItems">Reverse items</BitButton>
    </BitStack>
    <br />
    <div class="container short">
        <BitNavBar TItem="BitNavBarItem"
                   Mode="BitNavMode.Manual"
                   Items="dynamicNavBarItems"
                   @bind-SelectedItem="dynamicSelectedItem" />
    </div>
    <br />
    Selected item: @dynamicSelectedItem?.Text
</DemoExample>

<DemoExample Title="Cascading parameters" RazorCode="@example17RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example17CsharpCode" Id="example17" PreventRenderForMcpClient>
    <div>
        <b>BitParams</b> hands a <b>BitNavBarParams</b> to every navbar under it as defaults: a navbar keeps what it
        sets itself and takes only what it left unset. The object is not generic, so it serves all three item APIs.
    </div>
    <br />
    <BitParams Parameters="navBarParams">
        <div>Everything from the cascade:</div><br />
        <div class="container short">
            <BitNavBar Items="basicNavBarItems" DefaultSelectedItem="basicNavBarItems[0]" />
        </div>
        <br /><br />
        <div>Its own Indicator, the cascaded rest:</div><br />
        <div class="container short">
            <BitNavBar Items="basicNavBarItems" DefaultSelectedItem="basicNavBarItems[0]" Indicator="BitNavBarIndicator.Line" />
        </div>
    </BitParams>
    <br /><br />
    <div>Outside the cascade:</div><br />
    <div class="container short">
        <BitNavBar Items="basicNavBarItems" DefaultSelectedItem="basicNavBarItems[0]" Mode="BitNavMode.Manual" />
    </div>
</DemoExample>

